Fix discoverygarden/islandora_hocr v1.4.3: shipped Solr field type has solr_configs: null.

config/install/search_api_solr.solr_field_type.islandora_hocr_und_7_0_0.yml sets
`solr_configs: null`, but search_api_solr's schema types it as a mapping
(search_api_solr.solr_configs) and its own field types use `{}` or a mapping.
With NULL, SolrFieldType::getFieldTypeAsJson() and SolrFieldTypeForm::form()
log "Trying to access array offset on null" / "foreach() argument must be of
type array|object, null given", and config-set generation iterates the same
value. Ship an empty mapping instead. Still present on upstream main.

Only affects sites that install the module without existing config; sites that
already have the field type need their active config (and config/sync) fixed.

diff --git a/config/install/search_api_solr.solr_field_type.islandora_hocr_und_7_0_0.yml b/config/install/search_api_solr.solr_field_type.islandora_hocr_und_7_0_0.yml
index 7d54d40..2aacda0 100644
--- a/config/install/search_api_solr.solr_field_type.islandora_hocr_und_7_0_0.yml
+++ b/config/install/search_api_solr.solr_field_type.islandora_hocr_und_7_0_0.yml
@@ -89,5 +89,5 @@ field_type:
 unstemmed_field_type: null
 spellcheck_field_type: null
 collated_field_type: null
-solr_configs: null
+solr_configs: {  }
 text_files: {  }
